      {
        "id": 137283,
        "name": "MarioFanaticXV",
        "username": "MarioFanaticXV",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/{size}/2129_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-19T05:02:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"logan_mann\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/43a26b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> logan_mann:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is there anyway those maps could be posted high quality so that if we wanted to print them for ourselves to use we could try it? Maybe not, but it would be cool to try playing on some of these maps. Totally post the tournement its used of course.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I've only watched the first tournament thus far, but it seems to just be a single sheet with the tiles from the actual game printed onto a single sheet anyways, so there wouldn't be much point in that. You can even see the numbers identifying each tile if you look closely (though granted, I can't make out which number is which)- though you could just compare your own tiles to those used in the map, that'd probably be an easier way to rebuild it.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
